# A sequence this editor does not know, and a control byte it does not bind.
# Both say so on the message line rather than doing nothing: a key that does
# nothing and a key that was misread look the same to a person, and only one
# of them is a defect here.
#
# `esc Z` is a real escape sequence with an ending nothing binds; `ctrl A` is
# a control byte below 32 that is not one of the four the editor takes.
#
# **The message names the byte**, which it did not until the editor was first
# run under a real terminal: Ctrl-Q arrived as something else and `unknown
# key` could not say what. It was byte 4 -- `^D`, which `script` sends when
# its stdin closes and which raw mode delivers as an ordinary byte.
name keys.pas
size 6 20
push text
draw
esc Z
draw
keys .
draw
ctrl A
draw
